  "fields": {
    "title": "Brutalism",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Web brutalism is a design trend that can be traced back to Pascal Deville. In 2014, he began collecting what he considered brutalist websites on his eponymous ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://brutalistwebsites.com/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "website",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". These websites are characterised by their simple structure and the use of raw HTML elements that have been styled with little or no CSS and hardly use any Javascript. As a result, at first glance, these websites appear undesigned and unfinished when compared to most commercial websites, which today are hardly ever written in pure HTML, CSS or Javascript, but instead rely on various frameworks or templates. At the same time, their design can be best described as surprising, unadapted, direct and honest.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2LDXsjJ4yud8z1je0pBJjQ",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "blockquote",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "paragraph",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "»In its ruggedness and lack of concern to look comfortable or easy, Brutalism can be seen as a reaction by a younger generation to the lightness, optimism, and frivolity of today's webdesign.« ",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                },
                {
                  "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
                  "data": {
                    "target": {
                      "sys": {
                        "id": "6xOved5yfX8oo3wCYPPHnB",
                        "type": "Link",
                        "linkType": "Entry"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "[2]",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "superscript"
                        }
                      ],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Brutalist webdesign can therefore be understood not only as a visual style, but as a postmodern movement and alternative position to the popular striving for ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6UzOyP2ueyoyoD8IMtYciu",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "transparency and usability",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " in webdesign. By challenging familiar aesthetics and conventions, brutalist websites seek to create an individual experience tailored to the content of the site, rather than a transparent and therefore interchangeable interface. By keeping the underlying code of the websites simple, they make it easier for users to understand how the code works and that it was written manually by a person (who does not have to be a professional developer). Brutalist webdesign deliberately breaks with what can be called ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1a5QRShaM3BTIUyY1rsLkP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "generic template design",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ".",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2LDXsjJ4yud8z1je0pBJjQ",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "It is important to mention that the high period of web brutalism is over by now. The website ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://brutalistwebsites.com/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "www.brutalistwebsites.com",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " has not been updated for a few years and web brutalism seems to have not only lost its otherness and radicality, but also to have drifted further and further away from its original approach. Today, a milder visual form of brutalism, known as neobrutalism or ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://www.svgator.com/blog/neubrutalism-in-web-design-embracing-the-ugly/ "
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "neubrutalism",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", can be found on the mainstream web. Though this can be visually traced back to the web brutalism trend, it lacks a recognisable attitude.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Brutalism refers to an architectural style that has been popular between 1960 and the early 1980s. Buildings of this era can be recognised by their use of exposed concrete, simple geometric forms, emphasis on construction and deliberately rough finishing.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "EX2W47xO4ixu4P9Je7Z2w",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[3]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
